{"title":"Career Roadmap: School Counsellor","role":"School Counsellor","summary":"A School Counsellor supports students with academic, emotional, behavioural, social and career-related concerns within an educational setting.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Psychology"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build foundations in psychology, child/adolescent development, counselling skills, educational psychology, safeguarding, communication and supervised practical experience"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A School Counsellor supports students with academic, emotional, behavioural, social and career-related concerns within an educational setting."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Individual counselling"},{"text":"Group counselling"},{"text":"Student wellbeing programmes"},{"text":"Academic guidance"},{"text":"Career guidance"},{"text":"Behavioural support"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Teacher consultation"},{"text":"Student referrals"},{"text":"Crisis/safeguarding support"},{"text":"Social-emotional learning"},{"text":"Prevention and awareness programmes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A BA Psychology provides a useful foundation, but a bachelor's degree alone should not automatically be treated as equivalent to professional clinical-psychology qualification. For school counselling roles, employers may prefer or require postgraduate counselling/psychology qualifications, supervised experience, and specific credentials depending on the institution and jurisdiction."},{"type":"p","text":"For students targeting this career, the pathway should therefore be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Psychology","Psychology Foundation","Child & Adolescent Psychology","Counselling Skills","Educational Psychology","Practicum/Supervision","School Internship","Counselling Qualification/PG where required","School Counsellor"]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Psychology foundation"},{"text":"Developmental, social and cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Psychology notes + basic case analysis"},{"text":"Treating psychology as only theory"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Counselling foundation"},{"text":"Counselling theories, communication, child psychology"},{"text":"Role-play + supervised practice"},{"text":"Giving advice without assessment"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"School specialization"},{"text":"Educational psychology, adolescent wellbeing, safeguarding"},{"text":"School counselling project"},{"text":"No practical exposure"}],[{"text":"Year 4*"},{"text":"Advanced practice"},{"text":"Internship, case documentation, career guidance"},{"text":"Supervised practicum + portfolio"},{"text":"Working independently without supervision"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"*For a 4-year honours structure. In a 3-year programme, integrate the final-stage practicum and specialization into the third year."}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1 — Psychology Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to psychology"},{"text":"Biological bases of behaviour"},{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Emotion"},{"text":"Personality"},{"text":"Psychological research basics"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Critical thinking"},{"text":"Professional communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2 — Human Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Adolescence"},{"text":"Adult development"},{"text":"Cognitive development"},{"text":"Emotional development"},{"text":"Social development"},{"text":"Moral development"},{"text":"Attachment"},{"text":"Identity development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand developmental differences between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Childhood"},{"text":"Early adolescence"},{"text":"Middle adolescence"},{"text":"Late adolescence"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A school counsellor must understand that behaviour should be interpreted in the context of age and developmental stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3 — Counselling Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling principles"},{"text":"Therapeutic communication"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Empathy"},{"text":"Rapport building"},{"text":"Open-ended questions"},{"text":"Reflection"},{"text":"Paraphrasing"},{"text":"Summarization"},{"text":"Goal setting"},{"text":"Counselling boundaries"},{"text":"Professional ethics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand basic approaches such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Person-centred approach"},{"text":"Cognitive Behavioural Therapy concepts"},{"text":"Solution-focused approaches"},{"text":"Motivational interviewing concepts"},{"text":"Behavioural approaches"},{"text":"Strength-based approaches"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These should initially be learned as foundational frameworks, not as permission to independently treat mental-health disorders."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4 — Educational Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Learning theories"},{"text":"Classroom behaviour"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Academic performance"},{"text":"Learning difficulties"},{"text":"Peer relationships"},{"text":"Bullying"},{"text":"School adjustment"},{"text":"Family-school relationships"},{"text":"Teacher-student relationships"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Special educational needs awareness"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand factors affecting student performance:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Student","Family","School","Peer Group","Learning Environment","Community","Digital Environment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5 — Adolescent Counselling & Student Wellbeing"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adolescence"},{"text":"Identity"},{"text":"Self-esteem"},{"text":"Peer pressure"},{"text":"Academic stress"},{"text":"Examination anxiety"},{"text":"Family conflict"},{"text":"Bullying"},{"text":"Social media"},{"text":"Relationship concerns"},{"text":"Behavioural difficulties"},{"text":"School refusal"},{"text":"Career uncertainty"},{"text":"Emotional regulation"},{"text":"Decision-making"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to identify when a student needs:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Counselling","School support","Parent involvement","Specialist referral","Emergency intervention"]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6 — School Counselling Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intake"},{"text":"Basic psychosocial assessment"},{"text":"Goal setting"},{"text":"Session planning"},{"text":"Case documentation"},{"text":"Referral"},{"text":"Follow-up"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Teacher consultation"},{"text":"Group counselling"},{"text":"Student workshops"},{"text":"Career guidance"},{"text":"Wellbeing programmes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice creating:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student intake forms"},{"text":"Session plans"},{"text":"Referral templates"},{"text":"Progress notes"},{"text":"Parent communication templates"},{"text":"School wellbeing plans"}]},{"type":"p","text":"All student records must be handled confidentially and according to applicable institutional/legal requirements."}]},{"heading":"Child & Adolescent Psychology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A school counsellor should understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Cognitive"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Executive functioning"},{"text":"Decision-making"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emotional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Emotion regulation"},{"text":"Self-esteem"},{"text":"Anxiety"},{"text":"Frustration tolerance"},{"text":"Resilience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Social"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Peer relationships"},{"text":"Friendship"},{"text":"Social identity"},{"text":"Bullying"},{"text":"Group dynamics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Behavioural"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classroom behaviour"},{"text":"Reinforcement"},{"text":"Habit formation"},{"text":"Impulse control"},{"text":"School engagement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Family"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parenting styles"},{"text":"Family communication"},{"text":"Parent-child relationships"},{"text":"Family transitions"}]}]},{"heading":"Counselling Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"h","text":"Active Listening"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attending"},{"text":"Minimal encouragers"},{"text":"Clarification"},{"text":"Reflection"},{"text":"Paraphrasing"},{"text":"Summarization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Questioning"},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Open questions"},{"text":"Clarifying questions"},{"text":"Exploratory questions"},{"text":"Goal-focused questions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid turning counselling into an interrogation."},{"type":"h","text":"Rapport"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trust"},{"text":"Psychological safety"},{"text":"Respect"},{"text":"Non-judgmental communication"},{"text":"Appropriate boundaries"}]}]},{"heading":"Counselling Process","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A basic school-counselling workflow can be:"},{"type":"h","text":"Referral/Request"},{"type":"h","text":"Initial Conversation"},{"type":"h","text":"Concern Identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk & Safety Screening"},{"type":"h","text":"Goal Setting"},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling/Support"},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring"},{"type":"h","text":"Follow-up"},{"type":"h","text":"Closure or Referral"},{"type":"p","text":"Not every student concern requires long-term counselling."}]},{"heading":"Student Assessment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of psychological assessment without assuming that every test can be administered independently."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Behavioural observation"},{"text":"Rating scales"},{"text":"Screening tools"},{"text":"Academic assessments"},{"text":"Developmental assessments"},{"text":"Career-interest assessments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important principles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Validity"},{"text":"Norms"},{"text":"Standardization"},{"text":"Cultural appropriateness"},{"text":"Informed consent/assent where applicable"},{"text":"Confidentiality"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Only use psychological instruments within the scope of the counsellor's training, authorization and institutional policy."}]},{"heading":"Safeguarding & Child Protection","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a critical school-counselling competency."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child safety"},{"text":"Abuse awareness"},{"text":"Neglect"},{"text":"Bullying"},{"text":"Harassment"},{"text":"Online safety"},{"text":"Self-harm warning signs"},{"text":"Suicidal-risk awareness"},{"text":"Exploitation"},{"text":"Domestic violence awareness"},{"text":"Mandatory reporting requirements where applicable"},{"text":"School safeguarding procedures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A counsellor should know when confidentiality has limits because of imminent safety concerns, child-protection obligations or applicable law."},{"type":"p","text":"The correct response to a serious safety concern is not to manage it alone."},{"type":"flow","items":["Identify","Stabilize","Follow safeguarding protocol","Escalate/refer","Document appropriately"]}]},{"heading":"Mental-Health Referral","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A school counsellor should recognize situations that require specialist support."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential referral areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Severe depression symptoms"},{"text":"Significant anxiety"},{"text":"Eating-related concerns"},{"text":"Substance misuse"},{"text":"Psychosis-related symptoms"},{"text":"Serious behavioural problems"},{"text":"Trauma"},{"text":"Abuse"},{"text":"Self-harm"},{"text":"Suicidal thoughts or behaviour"},{"text":"Significant functional impairment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible referral network:"},{"type":"flow","items":["School Counsellor","Psychologist/Psychiatrist/Pediatrician/Specialist","Family/Guardian","Emergency services where necessary"]},{"type":"p","text":"A school counsellor should not independently diagnose or treat conditions outside their professional scope."}]},{"heading":"Career Counselling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"School counselling frequently overlaps with career guidance."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Career exploration"},{"text":"Interest assessment"},{"text":"Strength identification"},{"text":"Aptitude awareness"},{"text":"Subject selection"},{"text":"Course exploration"},{"text":"Career research"},{"text":"College planning"},{"text":"Employability skills"},{"text":"Goal setting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students can be supported through:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Self-understanding","Career exploration","Course mapping","Skill planning","Academic planning","Career action plan"]}]},{"heading":"Group Counselling & Workshops","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop programmes on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Study skills"},{"text":"Examination preparation"},{"text":"Stress management"},{"text":"Emotional regulation"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Peer relationships"},{"text":"Bullying prevention"},{"text":"Digital wellbeing"},{"text":"Career awareness"},{"text":"Goal setting"},{"text":"Time management"},{"text":"College preparation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Session design"},{"text":"Facilitation"},{"text":"Icebreakers"},{"text":"Group discussion"},{"text":"Activities"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Outcome measurement"}]}]},{"heading":"Parent & Teacher Collaboration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A school counsellor does not work with students in isolation."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to communicate professionally with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Parents"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student concerns"},{"text":"Progress"},{"text":"Support strategies"},{"text":"Referral recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Teachers"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classroom observations"},{"text":"Academic concerns"},{"text":"Behavioural observations"},{"text":"Student support plans"}]},{"type":"h","text":"School Leadership"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wellbeing programmes"},{"text":"Safeguarding"},{"text":"Student-support policies"},{"text":"Counselling utilization"},{"text":"Programme outcomes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Maintain appropriate confidentiality rather than unnecessarily sharing private student information."}]},{"heading":"School Counselling Data & Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to maintain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student intake records"},{"text":"Session notes"},{"text":"Referral records"},{"text":"Follow-up records"},{"text":"Workshop attendance"},{"text":"Programme evaluations"},{"text":"Aggregate wellbeing indicators"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"Secure school information systems"},{"text":"Forms/survey platforms"},{"text":"Power BI for de-identified aggregate reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not place identifiable student counselling information into unsecured spreadsheets or public AI tools."}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Student Wellbeing Programme"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a school programme covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stress management"},{"text":"Emotional regulation"},{"text":"Study skills"},{"text":"Peer relationships"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Needs assessment"},{"text":"Session plan"},{"text":"Activities"},{"text":"Evaluation questionnaire"},{"text":"Outcome report"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — School Counselling Case Simulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Create anonymized fictional cases involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic stress"},{"text":"Bullying"},{"text":"Peer pressure"},{"text":"Career uncertainty"},{"text":"Family conflict"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For each case document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Presenting concern"},{"text":"Initial observations"},{"text":"Support goals"},{"text":"Counselling approach"},{"text":"Referral considerations"},{"text":"Follow-up plan"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not use real student-identifiable information in a student portfolio."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Career Guidance Programme"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a programme for students covering:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Self-awareness","Interests","Strengths","Career exploration","Course selection","Action plan"]},{"type":"p","text":"Include a career-planning workbook and workshop presentation."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"School Student Wellbeing & Counselling Support System"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a simulated school counselling framework containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student wellbeing needs assessment"},{"text":"Counselling referral workflow"},{"text":"Appointment management"},{"text":"Session documentation structure"},{"text":"Career-guidance module"},{"text":"Parent/teacher referral process"},{"text":"Safeguarding escalation pathway"},{"text":"Workshop management"},{"text":"Aggregate wellbeing dashboard"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important"},{"type":"p","text":"The system should use fictional or fully de-identified data."},{"type":"p","text":"The capstone should demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology knowledge"},{"text":"Counselling workflow"},{"text":"Safeguarding awareness"},{"text":"Career guidance"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Data ethics"},{"text":"School administration"}]}]},{"heading":"Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Word"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Google Workspace"},{"text":"Digital forms"},{"text":"Presentation tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Survey tools"},{"text":"School information systems"},{"text":"Basic data analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted educational content"},{"text":"Digital wellbeing tools"},{"text":"AI-assisted career exploration"},{"text":"Student-support analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should not replace professional judgement, counselling relationships or safeguarding decisions."}]},{"heading":"Internships & Practical Experience","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"International schools"},{"text":"Special schools"},{"text":"Educational institutions"},{"text":"Student-support centres"},{"text":"Child-development organizations"},{"text":"NGOs working with children"},{"text":"Youth-development organizations"},{"text":"Career-counselling centres"},{"text":"Educational psychology settings"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize internships involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student observation"},{"text":"Counselling support"},{"text":"Workshops"},{"text":"Career guidance"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Student wellbeing"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Supervised practice"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For counselling work, supervision and appropriate scope of practice are more important than simply accumulating internship certificates."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful supplementary areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling skills"},{"text":"Child psychology"},{"text":"Adolescent psychology"},{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Career counselling"},{"text":"School counselling"},{"text":"Child safeguarding"},{"text":"Mental-health first aid"},{"text":"Suicide/self-harm awareness"},{"text":"Behaviour management"},{"text":"Special education awareness"},{"text":"Social-emotional learning"},{"text":"Psychological first aid"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certifications should be treated as supplementary unless a specific employer or professional body recognizes them as a formal requirement."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Realistic graduate-level roles may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling Assistant"},{"text":"Student Support Assistant"},{"text":"School Counselling Assistant"},{"text":"Student Wellbeing Coordinator"},{"text":"Student Support Coordinator"},{"text":"Behaviour Support Assistant"},{"text":"Career Guidance Assistant"},{"text":"Career Counselling Associate"},{"text":"Psychology Assistant"},{"text":"Child Development Programme Associate"},{"text":"Student Affairs Coordinator"},{"text":"Learning Support Assistant"},{"text":"Special Education Support Assistant"},{"text":"Youth Programme Associate"},{"text":"Mental-Health Programme Assistant"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the employer and qualifications, School Counsellor may be available directly after the relevant qualification, but many institutions prefer postgraduate training and supervised counselling experience."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For students seriously targeting school counselling, postgraduate study can significantly strengthen employability."},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Psychology"},{"text":"MSc Psychology"},{"text":"MA Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"MA Applied Psychology"},{"text":"MA Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Child Psychology-related programmes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Guidance & Counselling"},{"text":"School Counselling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Education"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Ed."},{"text":"M.Ed."},{"text":"Special Education programmes"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility varies considerably by institution and programme, so the specific admission requirements should be checked before selecting a pathway."},{"type":"h","text":"Important Distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"School counselling ≠ clinical psychology."},{"type":"p","text":"A person should not assume that a BA/MA Psychology automatically provides eligibility to practice as a regulated clinical psychologist. Professional titles, registration and scope of practice depend on the applicable professional regulations and qualifications."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential postgraduate fields include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"School Counselling"},{"text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Child & Adolescent Psychology"},{"text":"Student Affairs"},{"text":"Mental Health Counselling"},{"text":"Guidance & Counselling"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Applied Psychology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Before applying, verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Professional accreditation"},{"text":"Practicum requirements"},{"text":"Supervised hours"},{"text":"Registration requirements"},{"text":"Scope of practice"},{"text":"Background checks"},{"text":"International-student eligibility"},{"text":"Post-study work rules"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A foreign qualification does not automatically confer professional authorization to practice in another country."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"School Counselling Track"},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling/Student Support Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"School Counsellor"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior School Counsellor"},{"type":"h","text":"Lead Counsellor / Student Wellbeing Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"School Counselling Coordinator"},{"type":"h","text":"Head of Student Wellbeing / Pastoral Care"},{"type":"h","text":"Student Support / Wellbeing Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative Routes"},{"type":"flow","items":["Career Counselling","Career Guidance Lead","Career Services Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["Educational Psychology","Specialist Student Support","Educational Psychology roles"]},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["Child & Youth Services","Programme Coordinator","Programme Manager"]}]},{"heading":"Long-Term Relevance: 2030–2046","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Schools are likely to place increasing emphasis on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student mental wellbeing"},{"text":"Social-emotional learning"},{"text":"Digital wellbeing"},{"text":"Cyberbullying"},{"text":"Career uncertainty"},{"text":"AI-era career guidance"},{"text":"Learning difficulties"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Parent-school collaboration"},{"text":"Early identification and referral"},{"text":"Student resilience"},{"text":"Online safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Technology may support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student surveys"},{"text":"Wellbeing trend analysis"},{"text":"Career exploration"},{"text":"Administrative documentation"},{"text":"Resource personalization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But counselling will continue to depend heavily on:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human trust","empathy","professional judgement","safeguarding","ethical practice."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Social psychology"},{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Personality"},{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Child & adolescent psychology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Rapport"},{"text":"Counselling communication"},{"text":"Goal setting"},{"text":"Basic intervention frameworks"},{"text":"Group counselling"},{"text":"Career counselling"},{"text":"Referral"}]},{"type":"h","text":"School Practice"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Student wellbeing"},{"text":"Behaviour support"},{"text":"Academic support"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Teacher consultation"},{"text":"Safeguarding"},{"text":"Inclusive education"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Assessment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Screening principles"},{"text":"Psychometric fundamentals"},{"text":"Assessment ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Crisis escalation"},{"text":"Multidisciplinary collaboration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Digital forms"},{"text":"School information systems"},{"text":"Basic analytics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Responsible AI use"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Portfolio Target","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong psychology foundation"},{"text":"Child & adolescent psychology knowledge"},{"text":"Educational psychology 